   "text": "This is a resin-bound peptide: Fmoc-Arg(Pbf)-Ser(tBu)-Leu-Pro-Oic-Ile-Cys(Trt)-Ile, joined through its C-terminal carboxylate to the bead. I wrote the sequence from the N-terminus, so the SMILES starts at the Fmoc group and ends at the resin.\n\n**Residues, N-terminus to C-terminus:**\n- **Fmoc:** the fluorenylmethoxycarbonyl group on the Arg \u03b1-nitrogen.\n- **Arg(Pbf):** the guanidine nitrogen carries the Pbf sulfonyl group. Its ring has 2,2-dimethyl-dihydrobenzofuran fused to a trimethyl-substituted benzene.\n- **Ser(tBu):** the serine side chain is an O-tert-butyl ether.\n- **Leu:** an isobutyl side chain.\n- **Pro:** a plain pyrrolidine ring.\n- **Oic:** octahydroindole-2-carboxylic acid. I derived its three stereocentres from the wedges and hashes. The ring-fusion hydrogens are both hashed, so the ring fusion is cis, and the C2 carbonyl is a wedge.\n- **Ile:** isoleucine, with natural stereochemistry assumed.\n- **Cys(Trt):** the cysteine sulfur carries a trityl group (S\u2013C(Ph)\u2083).\n- **Ile (C-terminal):** isoleucine, esterified to the resin bead. I wrote the bead as a `*` atom.\n\nFor the Arg, Ser, Leu, Pro, Ile and Cys centres I assumed natural L-configuration rather than reading each wedge individually.\n\nSMILES: O=C(OCC1c2ccccc2-c2ccccc12)N[C@@H](CCCNC(=N)NS(=O)(=O)c1c(C)c(C)c2OC(C)(C)Cc2c1C)C(=O)N[C@@H](COC(C)(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)N1CCC[C@H]1C(=O)N1[C@H]2CCCC[C@H]2C[C@H]1C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)CC)C(=O)N[C@@H](CSC(c1ccccc1)(c1ccccc1)c1ccccc1)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)CC)C(=O)O*"
